Strips several admin UI sections that are no longer needed and clears the alert badge when an approval action is taken.

## Removed

- **Policies tab** — entire tab and content removed from `AdminDashboard`
- **7-Day Activity Trend** chart from Overview tab
- **Confidence Score** card from AI Risk analysis result (Risk Level label retained)
- **Risk Trend (30 days)**, **Daily Activities (30 days)**, **Activity Heatmap (30 days)** from Activities tab
- **Email Settings** and **System Health** nav links from `Navbar` and their routes from `App.jsx`

## Alert badge fix

`onUpdate` in the Approvals tab now calls `fetchAlerts()` and resets `unreadAlerts` to `0`, so the Alerts tab badge clears immediately after an approval or denial.

```jsx
onUpdate={() => {
  fetchApprovals();
  fetchLogs();
  fetchStats();
  fetchAlerts();
  setUnreadAlerts(0);
}}
```

The dlopen fallback path added in #96 uses all Mach-Os found under `Frameworks/` as candidates, bypassing the filtering that `resolveLoadCommand` normally applies (which ignores `@rpath/libswift*`). This can cause the injector to select a Swift runtime dylib as the injection target.

- Filter `allMachOsInFrameworks` in the fallback branch to exclude `libswift*` and `ignoredDylibAndFrameworkNames` entries before sorting/selection

```swift
let filteredMachOs = allMachOsInFrameworks.filter { url in
    let nameLower = url.lastPathComponent.lowercased()
    if nameLower.hasPrefix("libswift") {
        return false
    }
    if Self.ignoredDylibAndFrameworkNames.contains(nameLower) {
        return false
    }
    return true
}
```

Four independent bugs across upload flow, realtime subscriptions, and album management.

## UploadModal — stale state on reopen (`UploadModal.tsx`)
`handleClose` revoked blob URLs but left `files` (and all other form fields) intact. Since the component stays mounted behind `isOpen`, reopening showed broken `<img>` previews (revoked blob URLs) and leftover form data. `handleClose` now resets all fields before calling `onClose()`.

## Notification bell badge not realtime (`Navbar.tsx`)
`unreadCount` was fetched once on auth change and never updated. Added an `INSERT` listener on `notifications` to the existing Supabase channel:
```ts
.on('postgres_changes', { event: 'INSERT', schema: 'public', table: 'notifications' },
  (payload) => {
    if (payload.new.user_id === user.id && !payload.new.read) {
      setUnreadCount(n => n + 1);
    }
  })
```

## Messages list has no realtime updates (`app/messages/page.tsx`)
The conversations list was fetch-once; new messages didn't reorder or update the last-message preview. Added a second `useEffect` subscribing to `messages` INSERT and `conversations` UPDATE, re-running `loadConversations` on each event with proper channel cleanup.

## Album `manageMode` not reset when last photo removed (`app/album/[id]/page.tsx`)
Deleting the last photo hid the toggle button but left `manageMode = true`. Fixed in the `setPhotos` updater:
```ts
setPhotos(prev => {
  const next = prev.filter(p => p.id !== photoId);
  if (next.length === 0) setManageMode(false);
  return next;
});
```

